{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityGroupRank","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityGroupRank","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.Rank","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.atomicity_group_rank_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.atomicity_group_rank_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L165-L176","doc":"**Atomicity exact group rank (conditional).** For `G` whose Lie algebra is a subalgebra\n`𝔤 ⊆ 𝔰𝔩₂`, *if* `rank G = rank Lie(G)` then `rank G = 1`. Fed the landed exact Lie-side\nvalue `LieAlgebra.rank K 𝔤 = 1` (discharged sorry-free by\n`QOU.Atomicity.sl2_rank_eq_one`, PR #4285, threaded here as a hypothesis). The\ngroup-rank premise `RankGroupEqRankLie K 𝔤 G` is **OPEN**; only this implication is proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.groupRank_eq_of_lieRank_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.groupRank_eq_of_lieRank_eq","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L153-L163","doc":"**Exact group rank (conditional).** If `rank G = rank Lie(G)` and the Lie-algebra\nrank is exactly `n`, then the group rank is exactly `n`. The equality-direction companion\nof `groupRank_le_of_lieRank_le`; a direct rewrite by the class field. Fully proved modulo\nthe class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.atomicity_group_rank_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.atomicity_group_rank_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L134-L151","doc":"**Atomicity group-rank upper bound (conditional).** For the Tannaka dual `G` whose\nLie algebra is a subalgebra `𝔤 ⊆ 𝔰𝔩₂`, *if* `rank G = rank Lie(G)` (the open premise\n`RankGroupEqRankLie K 𝔤 G`), then `rank G ≤ 1`.\n\n**What is proved vs. open.** The implication is proved sorry-free: it is\n`groupRank_le_of_lieRank_le` fed the landed Lie-side bound `hLie`. The bound `hLie`\nitself — `LieAlgebra.rank K 𝔤 ≤ 1` — is discharged sorry-free by\n`QOU.Atomicity.sl2_subalgebra_rank_le_one h2 𝔤` (landed, PR #4285) and is threaded here\nas an explicit hypothesis to keep this file decoupled from that in-flight branch. The\n**group-rank premise** `RankGroupEqRankLie K 𝔤 G` is **OPEN** — no instance exists; this\nis a conditional result, not a closure of atomicity on the group side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.groupRank_le_of_lieRank_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.groupRank_le_of_lieRank_le","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L122-L132","doc":"**General conditional bound.** If `rank G = rank Lie(G)` (the open premise, as the\nclass `RankGroupEqRankLie R L G`) and the Lie-algebra rank is `≤ n`, then the group rank\nis `≤ n`. Fully proved modulo the class — a rigorous conditional. The Lie-rank bound\n`hLie` is the input the Lie-side development supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankGroupEqRankLie.rank_group_eq_rank_lie","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankGroupEqRankLie.rank_group_eq_rank_lie","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L118-L118","doc":"The genuine content: the algebraic-group rank equals the Lie-algebra rank.\nThis is the open premise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankGroupEqRankLie.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankGroupEqRankLie.mk","kind":"ctor","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankGroupEqRankLie","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankGroupEqRankLie","kind":"class","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L94-L118","doc":"**Conditional class (§3b-cond): `rank G = rank Lie(G)`.** This is the standard\nstructural theorem identifying the rank of an algebraic group `G` with the rank of its\nLie algebra `L = Lie(G)`, **absent from Mathlib** (see the survey above). We axiomatize\nit as a `Prop`-valued class whose single field is the **genuine equality**\n`groupRank G = LieAlgebra.rank R L` — *not* `True`, and *not* the block's own conclusion.\n\nThe equality is non-trivial to discharge: `groupRank G` is fixed independently by the\n`AlgebraicGroupRank G` instance (it does not mention `L`), so an instance of this class\nmust actually *prove* that the group's maximal-torus dimension equals the Lie-algebra\ngeneric-`ad`-nullity — the whole content of the theorem. Establishing that in general\nrequires the maximal-torus / Lie-functor theory Mathlib lacks.\n\n**OPEN PREMISE — no canonical instance is provided.** Per the anti-laundering rule\n(`AGENTS.md §\"Axiomatization is NOT a Proof\"`), writing this class does **not** prove\n`rank G = rank Lie(G)`; the theorem remains mathematically open in this corpus. Any\ndownstream result depending on it is a *rigorous conditional* (proved modulo this class),\nnever an unconditional claim.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] rank G = rank Lie(G); see file docstring for standard references. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.groupRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.groupRank","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L90-L92","doc":"The rank of an algebraic group `G`, once `G` carries an `AlgebraicGroupRank` handle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.AlgebraicGroupRank.groupRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.AlgebraicGroupRank.groupRank","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The rank of `G` (dimension of a maximal torus). Supplied by the ambient\nalgebraic-group theory; abstract here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.AlgebraicGroupRank.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.AlgebraicGroupRank.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.AlgebraicGroupRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.AlgebraicGroupRank","kind":"class","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityGroupRank.lean#L75-L88","doc":"**Abstract algebraic-group rank (data).** Mathlib has no maximal-torus-of-an-algebraic-\ngroup theory, so the rank of an algebraic group `G` — the common dimension of its maximal\ntori — cannot be constructed here. We carry it as *opaque data*: `[AlgebraicGroupRank G]`\nmeans \"`G` comes equipped with a well-defined rank `groupRank G : ℕ`\". This is a data\nclass (like `Fintype` carrying `card`), **not** a proposition — it makes no unproved\nlogical claim; it only names a quantity the ambient algebraic-group theory would supply.\n\nThis is the honest placeholder for the missing Mathlib API. It is deliberately weak: it\nasserts nothing about how `groupRank G` relates to anything, so it cannot be used to\nlaunder a claim. The load-bearing relation lives in `RankGroupEqRankLie` below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}